재활용 리스트 뷰.\n- 템플릿 노드 하나와 항목 수만 받아, 화면에 보:
Recycling list view.
- Takes just one template node and an item count, creates real nodes only for the visible range, and
  reclaims and reuses nodes that go out of range. Even with hundreds ~ thousands of items, the node count stays at one screen's worth.
- Attaches to the same node as UIScrollView. (auto-attached via require)
  Item content is filled in code with setBindItemEvent. (data-driven)
- When it nears the end, it sends a setReachEndEvent notification once. (infinite scroll / load more)
  When the item count grows via setItemCount, the notification is re-armed.
- Instead of a template, you can give a function that creates item nodes (setCreateItemEvent). If the item size is not set, it reads the size of the first created item.
- Usage:
    const listView = scrollNode.addComponent(UIListView);
    listView.setTemplateNode(templateNode);
    listView.setBindItemEvent((itemNode, itemIndex) => { ... });
    listView.setItemCount(500);
    listView.setReachEndEvent(() => { ... });

창 층. (영역 위에 UIWindow 를 쌓는다)\n- 창을 띄우면 맨:
Window layer. (stacks UIWindow over the area)
- Opening a window stacks it on top, and only the top window is visible. When the upper window closes, the window below is visible again.
- Closing removes it from the list immediately so presses and covering are released at once, and it is detached after the close motion (PopupMotion) finishes.
  Closing a window that was covered detaches it immediately without motion.
- This layer is enlarged by the UI scale (UIScale.read), and windows are notified of the area size and safe area width divided by that amount. (so text is readable even on small screens)
  With setUIScaleOptions(null) it does not enlarge.
- While even one window is open, play is suspended. It notifies when windows open and close (setWindowChangeEvent), so the game pauses and resumes play.
- The top window receives the wheel first (UIWindow.handleWheel), and if it does not handle it, the scroll view at that position. GameScene passes wheel input pointing inside the window layer to scrollWindowAt.
- Usage: (place it as the topmost child of the area node, and notify it whenever the area size changes)
    const windowLayer = new UIWindowLayer();
    playAreaNode.addChild(windowLayer);
    windowLayer.setViewSize(playAreaWidth, playAreaHeight);
    windowLayer.setViewBleed(insets.top, insets.right, insets.bottom, insets.left);
    windowLayer.setWindowChangeEvent(() => { game.setPaused(windowLayer.hasOpenWindow()); });
    windowLayer.openWindow(new UIConfirmWindow("quit", { title: "Quit", message: "Do you really want to quit?" }));

컨텍스트 메뉴. (우클릭 / 길게 누름 메뉴)\n- show(positi:
Context menu. (right-click / long-press menu)
- show(position, itemList) pops up the item list at that position.
  Pressing outside closes it, and pressing an item calls its handler and closes it.
- addChild it at the top (last child) of the scene root before use.
- Usage:
    const contextMenu = new UIContextMenu();
    scene.getRoot().addChild(contextMenu);
    contextMenu.show(viewPosition, [
        { text: "Copy", handler: () => {} },
        { text: "Delete", handler: () => {} },
    ]);

타임라인.\n- 문서(서술)는 무대 노드 목록 + 트랙(대상 이름 / 속:
Timeline.
- The document (description) is JSON made of a stage node list + tracks (target name / property / keys) + markers, and the timeline editor saves it.
- Create the stage nodes with buildStage(), or attach by name to an existing node tree with bind().
- A key's easing applies to the segment from that key to the next key.
- Usage:
    const timeline = await Timeline.loadFromUrl("./assets/intro.timeline.json");
    timeline.buildStage(stageNode, (imageName) => imageTable[imageName]);
    timeline.play();
    // every frame: timeline.tick(timeDelta);

타자기 연출 러너.\n- Text / UILabel 처럼 setVisib:
Typewriter effect runner.
- Reveals the characters of a target that has setVisibleCharacterCount(), such as Text / UILabel,
  one at a time at a given rate per second. (visual novel / RPG dialogue effect)
- Usage:
    const typewriter = new Typewriter(label, { charactersPerSecond: 30 });
    typewriter.start("Hello. The adventure begins.");
    // every frame: typewriter.tick(timeDelta);
    // on input: typewriter.isFinished() ? next() : typewriter.skipToEnd();
- Characters are counted in grapheme clusters (syllable-final consonants, combining marks and emoji clusters count as one character). The character reveal callback receives (grapheme cluster, index).

토스트.\n- show(message) 로 알약 모양 알림이 아래에서 떠:
Toast.
- show(message) makes a pill-shaped notification rise from the bottom, stay briefly, then disappear.
- Calling it several times queues them and shows them one by one. (a pattern several games copy-pasted per screen)
- addChild it at the top (last child) of the scene root before use.
- Usage:
    const toast = new UIToast();
    scene.getRoot().addChild(toast);
    toast.show("Saved.");

트레일 렌더러.\n- 노드가 지나간 자리를 점으로 기록해 굵기 / 색이:
Trail renderer.
- Records the path the node has passed as points and draws it as a band whose width / color fade out.
  (2D counterpart of Unity's TrailRenderer)
- Usage:
    const trail = node.addComponent(TrailRenderer);
    trail.setTime(0.5);
    trail.setWidth(14, 0);
    trail.setColors(new Color(0.4, 0.8, 1, 0.9), new Color(0.4, 0.8, 1, 0));

파티클 시스템.\n- 유니티 ParticleSystem 의 자주 쓰는 부:
Particle system.
- A component that ports the commonly used parts of Unity's ParticleSystem to 2D.
  Supports emission (rate / burst), shape, start ranges for lifetime / speed / size / rotation / color,
  size / color / rotation over lifetime, gravity / damping, additive blending, and image sprites.
- Usage:
    const particleSystem = node.addComponent(ParticleSystem);
    particleSystem.setEmissionRate(40);
    particleSystem.setStartLifetime(0.6, 1.2);
    particleSystem.setStartSpeed(40, 120);
    particleSystem.setColorOverLifetime([
        { time: 0, color: new Color(1, 0.8, 0.3, 1) },
        { time: 1, color: new Color(1, 0.2, 0, 0) },
    ]);
    particleSystem.play();

플랫포머 물리 컴포넌트.\n- 중력 적분 + 바닥 접지 + 좌우 이동 경:
Platformer physics component.
- Holds the minimal physics (kinematics) that side-scrollers kept reinventing, such as gravity integration + ground contact +
  horizontal movement bounds. Moves the node's local position directly.
- Usage:
    const body = node.addComponent(PlatformerBody);
    body.setGroundY(560);
    body.setHorizontalBounds(40, 920);
    // move: body.setVelocityX(±speed), jump: body.jump(-720)

화면 효과. (씬 후처리 사슬)\n- 씬은 화면에 그대로 그리고, end:
Screen effect. (scene post-processing chain)
- The scene draws to the screen as is, and end() captures the screen (or the region set with setRegion), applies the enabled effects in order, and puts it back in the same place.
- The region is in canvas pixel coordinates (top-left origin), and if a rounded corner radius is given, the original is kept outside it.
- Usage:
    // in the scene's load
    this.screenEffect = new ScreenEffect();
    this.screenEffect.setEnabled(ScreenEffectType.vignette, true);
    // at the start of preDraw / the end of postDraw
    this.screenEffect.begin(graphic);  ...  this.screenEffect.end(graphic);
    // in tick
    this.screenEffect.tick(timeDelta);

확인 대화 상자.\n- 어둡게 가리는 막 + 가운데 카드 + 확인 / 취:
Confirmation dialog.
- Pops up a darkening overlay + a centered card + confirm / cancel buttons with a single show().
  Entrance / exit animate with PopupMotion (bounce scale up / shrink).
- Pressing the overlay counts as cancel. If onCancel is not passed, it becomes a confirm-only alert.
- addChild it at the top (last child) of the scene root before use.
- Usage:
    const dialog = new UIDialog();
    scene.getRoot().addChild(dialog);
    dialog.show("Really delete?", { onConfirm: () => remove(), onCancel: () => {} });

확인 창. (제목, 묻는 글, 취소와 확인 두 단추)\n- UIWindo:
Confirm window. (title, question text, two buttons: cancel and confirm)
- Being a UIWindow, it is opened with UIWindowLayer. The question text wraps at the panel width and the panel height is set by the number of lines.
  If the text is long and exceeds the area height, only the text box scrolls and the two buttons are always visible.
- The buttons are cancel on the left and confirm (emphasized) on the right. For right-to-left languages (setRightToLeft) the order is reversed.
- Pressing confirm closes it after the confirm notification. Closing via cancel, pressing outside, closeTopWindow or closeAllWindows gives the cancel notification.
- The panel look is the same as UIWindow. Button and text colors are changed by getting the nodes with getConfirmButtonNode() and the like.
- Usage:
    const confirmWindow = new UIConfirmWindow("quit", { title: "Quit", message: "Do you really want to quit?", cancelText: "Cancel", confirmText: "Quit" });
    confirmWindow.setConfirmEvent(() => { leave(); });
    windowLayer.openWindow(confirmWindow);

회전 로딩 인디케이터.\n- 원 둘레에 점 여러 개를 놓고 밝기가 꼬리처:
Spinning loading indicator.
- A standard spinner with several dots around a circle whose brightness rotates like a tail.
- Usage:
    const spinner = new UISpinner({ radius: 9, dotCount: 10 });
    someNode.addChild(spinner);
    spinner.setLocalPosition(Vector2.create(x, y));

스프라이트 애니메이터 컴포넌트.\n- 이름을 붙인 클립(프레임 시퀀스)을:
Sprite animator component.
- Registers named clips (frame sequences) and switches with SpriteAnimator.play(node, "run") or playClip("run").
- Playing the same clip again does not restart it. (can be changed with the restartIfSame option)
- When a clip ends, the next state can follow via the onComplete callback. (combines with an FSM)
- Applies the current frame (image + rect) to the Sprite component on the same node.
- Usage:
    const animator = node.addComponent(SpriteAnimator);
    animator.addClip("idle", image, idleRects, 10, true);
    animator.addClip("attack", image, attackRects, 12, false);
    SpriteAnimator.play(node, "attack", { onComplete: () => animator.playClip("idle") });
- Same form in both engines: the static SpriteAnimator.play(node, clipName, options) plays with the node's animator, and playClip is for when only the animator is at hand (inside the complete callback).
  (the Rust SpriteAnimator::play, play_clip)
